# <%= current_page.data.title %>

The GOV.UK Content API is a public, read-only API for retrieving the content and
metadata of pages published on the [GOV.UK][gov-uk] website. This API returns the
same content published on the GOV.UK website that is available to any member of
the public, but in a format that your services, tools and products can consume
directly.

The GOV.UK Content API is owned and maintained by the Government Digital Service.​

Brief outline of what the docs contain (few bullets).

## What you can do with this API

The GOV.UK Content API returns structured data in [JSON][json-def] format,
providing a more accessible and predictable interface than scraping HTML from
web pages. You can use this API for building services, tools and products which
incorporate content from GOV.UK, and for keeping that content up to date.

Links in the API response allow you to navigate between related GOV.UK content.
For example, from one page you can see the government organisation who published
the page, then retrieve the policies of that organisation.

Our [API reference][api-reference] describes the API endpoints and response format
you can expect.

## What you can't do with this API

The content and metadata you can access using the GOV.UK Content API is limited
to pages on the [GOV.UK][gov-uk] website. This **does not include** pages on
other websites that are subdomains of `gov.uk`.

### Included

The following are examples of pages which you can access using the GOV.UK
Content API:

- [https://www.gov.uk/when-do-the-clocks-change]
- [https://www.gov.uk/self-assessment-tax-returns/registering]
- [https://www.gov.uk/browse/education]

### Not included

The following are examples of pages which you **cannot** access using the GOV.UK
Content API:

- [https://naturalengland.blog.gov.uk/2026/10/23/transforming-towns-and-cities-for-people-and-nature/]
- [https://payments.service.gov.uk/using-govuk-pay/]

Note no search, no full exports, no standalone attachments/images, no dynamic content.

This API includes only the pages on GOV.UK that are available as HTML and does
not allow direct access to attachments or images. These files however are
associated with their HTML content and can be accessed.

Not all content is available. For example, content that is generated
dynamically (such as through a search) is not available. Some types of content
may still be being migrated to utilise this API and these could appear
as placeholder documents without any content or as redirections to a
catch-all content item that represents a group of unmigrated content.

If you wish to access historic content this can currently be done
through the [National Archives][national-archives].

## Who can use this API

Anyone can use this API for any purpose. There is no need for onboarding or
signing any agreements.

